      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;resources-for-students&#34;&gt;Resources for students&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The mixer is available at &lt;a href=&#34;https://composingatmospheres.ro/mixer&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;
  composingatmospheres.ro/mixer
&lt;/a&gt; and you can play around to create your sounds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To play a cell, press the &lt;strong&gt;play&lt;/strong&gt; button. For each cell you have &lt;strong&gt;volume&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;panning&lt;/strong&gt; (left, right) controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1GniWG-FP7ZKbSEtPcKGtz0DEHewvg_cK?usp=sharing&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;
  Here
&lt;/a&gt; is a drive with &lt;code&gt;.wav&lt;/code&gt; files of the sounds that are in the mixer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can try &lt;a href=&#34;https://opendaw.org/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;
  this online DAW
&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.audacityteam.org/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;
  Audacity
&lt;/a&gt;, simple DAWs to try out your ideas.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
